Offset a menu section by the stripe width

The separator branch of a menu item paints the stripe of the menu across
the whole row. It then offsets the faded rule by the stripe width, and
it offsets nothing else. The header bevel of a section row therefore
covers the stripe, and the title of a section with no bevel lands on the
stripe.

The header and the title now take a rectangle that starts after the
stripe, as the faded rule does. The stripe stands clear of the section
row under both section styles. A menu with no stripe keeps the paint of
before.

The change sits on the branch work/style-paint of the local tree, as commit 19 of 21.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

